-- L4 names that land on the interview's OTHER two top-level namespaces.
--
-- M2 closed one third of this hazard (`l4runtime`'s star-import; see
-- `docassemble-runtime-collision.l4`) and left the two larger thirds open:
--
--   * PYTHON BUILTINS. A driver's `if all:` execs in the user_dict, whose
--     `__builtins__` Python injects automatically. `'all' in user_dict` is
--     False, but `eval('all', user_dict)` returns the built-in, so docassemble
--     never raises NameError and never backchains to the code block that would
--     have defined it. The function object is truthy, the driver takes the
--     "holds" branch, NO QUESTION IS ASKED AT ALL, and the fidelity report says
--     `(nothing lost)`. Measured against real docassemble 1.10.7 on the
--     unreserved spelling: `screen='All: Holds'`, `questions asked=[]`, against
--     an L4 `#EVAL` of FALSE.
--   * `docassemble.base.util`. `parse.py:131` compiles
--     `from docassemble.base.util import *` and `Interview.assemble` execs it
--     into the user_dict on every pass unless the interview sets `imports_util`
--     (parse.py:8523-8524). The emitter deliberately keeps that module out of
--     `modules:` so the auto-import still happens, so this cannot be avoided by
--     emitting differently. `Today` was measured the same way, and it is worse
--     than the builtins case: the name is in the user_dict for real, so
--     `reconsider:`'s deletion does not rescue it either.
--
-- Expect `all_` and `today_`, and no bare `all`/`today` in a variable position.

DECLARE Facts
    HAS
      @desc whether the box on the form was ticked
      `the box was ticked` IS A BOOLEAN

@export whether the builtin-shadowing rule holds
GIVEN f IS A Facts @desc The facts under assessment
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `All` f IF f's `the box was ticked`

@export whether the util-shadowing rule holds
GIVEN f IS A Facts @desc The facts under assessment
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Today` f IF f's `the box was ticked`

#EVAL `All` OF Facts WITH `the box was ticked` IS FALSE
-- FALSE

#EVAL `Today` OF Facts WITH `the box was ticked` IS FALSE
-- FALSE
